  "name": "Sealed vault",
  "description": "A slab door with a gold seal still unbroken on it and a slot cut under the seal. Shut, and drawn shut: no hinge, no handle, nothing that suggests it opens often \u2014 the find makes ruins rarer, and a door you could walk through would have said the opposite. The seal is the only warm thing on a grey plate, which is where the other half of the trade is: what is behind this one is worth more than what is behind the rest.",
